}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Teal Egg: N102''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Catarzan''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Catarzan is a simple unit, a midrange Area Attacker with good stats and strong against a trait; similar to [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]], but with lower range in exchange for Area Attack. His attacks are also non-stop, with 100% of the attack delay being backswing, so while he is less reliable as a pusher, you won't endanger him by placing him near the frontlines.

Catarzan is best stacked up behind meatshields, but can hold a bit if the line falls. Thanks to his Behemoth Slayer, he can control hordes of Behemoths even better, although his price and medium health keep him from being a safe bet in all situations.

Unfortunately, Catarzan gets outclassed by other anti-Alien attackers like [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] and [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]], while they may have worse range, they outperform Catarzan in terms of DPS against Alien enemies (9,450/16,065 > 2,009). And to make the matter worse, [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] outperforms him as an anti-Behemoth midranger. So there's no point of unlocking this True Form unless you have Behemoth Stones to spare or somewhat lack of anti-Alien attacker.

